{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/654799-demon-translation-guide-lores-without-torment-or-faith","id":654799,"title":"Demon Translation Guide: Lores without Torment or Faith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-06T23:43:07-07:00","id":654799,"title":"Demon Translation Guide: Lores without Torment or Faith","content":"Again, looking through the translation guide, I see the guidelines for converting Lores to Embeds/Exploits. Looks great, except I don't see a way to translate mechanics that call on spending Faith / rolling against Torment in such a way as to exclude those mechanics. I'm basically using the translation guide to port powers straight over into Descent, without trying to port or use any of Fallen's mechanics.<br /> <br /> Suggestions? Am I just missing a relevant section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T00:00:05-07:00","id":654823,"title":"","content":"If the Lore power becomes an Embed, there's no cost at all, even if the Lore power had one.<br /> If the Lore power becomes an Exploit, I'd say eyeball the cost compared to similarly powerful existing Exploits, default to 1 Aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T05:25:14-07:00","id":655036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/654799-demon-translation-guide-lores-without-torment-or-faith#post654799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suggestions? Am I just missing a relevant section?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that I noticed when I was recently rereading the core book. In a lot of cases, when you opt to drop an Embed like Combustion into a dramatic failure? The power still activates, but its not in your control - in the case of Combustion, your target immediately flares up into flames, despite rolling a failure. And dark/out of control is really the hallmark of using Torment powers, imho. So, I would use those rules to simulate Torment Lores through Embeds/Exploits. <br /> <br /> There's no equivalent to a Torment track, but we do have Conditions (a variation of Demonic Rage and Demonic Disconnect?) as well as Compromise checks. I'm not entirely sure on what the Torment track did mechanically, but I would definitely use Persistant Conditions that grow in severity, and potentially fade. <br /> <br /> So, in short. When translating Lores into Embeds/Exploits, the Torment part becomes the Dramatic Failure part. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T05:43:43-07:00","id":655042,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>I also considered using a Compromise when Torment is called for. Switched Temp Faith for Aether.</li> </ul><br /> Mind you, in the theoretical cross-over game the Fallen &amp; the Unchained are different kinds of creatures; close enough so that they can learn the 'lesser' abilities (Lores &amp; Embeds) of the others without issue (though at 'unfavoured' rates) but different enough so that things get kind of wonky and the more 'advanced' abilities (Rituals, Summonings/True Name compels, Paragon/Mastery of Lores &amp; Exploits) have an alarming tendency to backfire if they work at all.<br /> Said theoretical game places the two kinds of Demon in separate 'splinters' of reality. Waiting on C20, CtL 2nd and translation guide before attempting the appropriate homebrew fixes and full setting construction. CWoD/NWoD cross overs are tricky enough, anything that lightens my load...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}